<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?><?xml-stylesheet href="http://www.blogger.com/styles/atom.css" type="text/css"?><feed xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom' xmlns:openSearch='http://a9.com/-/spec/opensearchrss/1.0/' xmlns:gd="http://schemas.google.com/g/2005"><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post116413198123573982..comments</id><updated>2017-04-13T04:47:21.148-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Comments on Pro Libertate: Review of the News, November 21</title><link rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#feed' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/feeds/comments/default'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/116413198123573982/comments/default'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/11/review-of-news-november-21.html'/><link rel="hub" href="http://pubsubhubbub.appspot.com/"/><author><name>William N. Grigg</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/14368220509514750246</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='32' height='19' src='http://3.bp.blogspot.com/-5rhFUXs_62I/VgVL2E3rMII/AAAAAAAAMJ4/cjJOyI7W208/s220/Photo%2BRon%2BPaul%2BLiberty%2BReport.jpg'/></author><generator version='7.00' uri='http://www.blogger.com'>Blogger</generator><openSearch:totalResults>4</openSearch:totalResults><openSearch:startIndex>1</openSearch:startIndex><openSearch:itemsPerPage>25</openSearch:itemsPerPage><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-116420648160028268</id><published>2006-11-22T07:41:00.000-07:00</published><updated>2006-11-22T07:41:00.000-07:00</updated><title type='text'>Thanks for mentioning my partner Philip&#39;s book.  A...</title><content type='html'>Thanks for mentioning my partner Philip&#39;s book.  &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;As for opposing the draft on principle, actually he (and I) do.  We believe that when the nation&#39;s defense (as it probably did in both World Wars) requires military conscription, it can be resorted to, but what is done in extremis is not a binding precedent in normal situations.  As we are famously told, the Constitution is not a suicide pact:  the United  States is not immortal.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;With the Founders, we do believe that military service is an inherent and unalienable part of citizenship:  that citizens must participate in the common defense, but the means of participation should be chosen by the individual and change throughout their lifetime.  (We&#39;re not talking about 20 years in the reserves here.)  This includes everything from a tour in the federal forces to time in the state militias, to volunteer work in the neighborhood watch, as a firefighter, or in Search and Rescue.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;For more information, you might take a look at his website, www.philipgold.org.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Happy Thanksgiving,&lt;BR/&gt;Erin Solaro</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/116413198123573982/comments/default/116420648160028268'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/116413198123573982/comments/default/116420648160028268'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/11/review-of-news-november-21.html?showComment=1164206460000#c116420648160028268' title=''/><author><name>Anonymous</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/11/review-of-news-november-21.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-116413198123573982' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/116413198123573982' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-262634513"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="November 22, 2006 at 7:41 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-116417325548953477</id><published>2006-11-21T22:27:00.000-07:00</published><updated>2006-11-21T22:27:00.000-07:00</updated><title type='text'>chat..,you are on the money.  but you do not have ...</title><content type='html'>chat..,&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;you are on the money.  but you do not have to turn to DW for an answer.  according to the constitution, congress can raise an army.  that does not mean conscript an army.  the govt always called for volunteers until lincoln.  so how does congress draft men now?  the answer is on the back of your selective service card--they get you by your SSN.  no SSN? then you&#39;re not getting a govt benefit. no govt benefit? no requirement to serve.  the kicker here is that our parents put us in the social security system and the SSA will not let you out.  ron paul introduced legisaltion some time back to address this issue, but of course, like most of his pro-freedom initiatives, it got nowhere.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;however, i do believe ths to be true.  iraq and afghanistan have shown the public what 4th gen warfare is all abot, and that any draft for those to attend...will be met with violence to resist from being blown up by an IED.  maybe i&#39;m wrong?&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;oh.  funny how long we&#39;ve had the 13th amendment, yet it didn&#39;t stop the drafts for every war after its approval.  i&#39;m not too optimistic on that one.  the courts work for the govt you know.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/116413198123573982/comments/default/116417325548953477'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/116413198123573982/comments/default/116417325548953477'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/11/review-of-news-november-21.html?showComment=1164173220000#c116417325548953477' title=''/><author><name>rick</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/12473173027048173880</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/11/review-of-news-november-21.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-116413198123573982' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/116413198123573982' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-870704727"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="November 21, 2006 at 10:27 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-116414017362432048</id><published>2006-11-21T13:16:00.000-07:00</published><updated>2006-11-21T13:16:00.000-07:00</updated><title type='text'>The book, &quot;Leviathan at War&quot;, edited by Edmund Opi...</title><content type='html'>The book, &quot;Leviathan at War&quot;, edited by Edmund Opitz, had a chapter containing a speech by Daniel Webster given before the US House of Representatives in 1814. He correctly claims that &quot;Conscription&quot; is Unconstitutional because it was never authorized by the Constitution. Note that this was well before the 13th Amendment.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;I quoted heavily from it in a letter to the editor, reprinted here:&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;http://www.achattanoogawhig.com/id8.html&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Will - keep up the fantastic work! Please keep us up to date on the book you&#39;re working on and your efforts to launch your magazine. Will you be able to use &quot;The Review of the News&quot; as the title?</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/116413198123573982/comments/default/116414017362432048'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/116413198123573982/comments/default/116414017362432048'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/11/review-of-news-november-21.html?showComment=1164140160000#c116414017362432048' title=''/><author><name>A Radical Whig in Chattanooga</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/08489464838153487468</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/11/review-of-news-november-21.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-116413198123573982' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/116413198123573982' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-58288372"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="November 21, 2006 at 1:16 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-116413413695395078</id><published>2006-11-21T11:35:00.000-07:00</published><updated>2006-11-21T11:35:00.000-07:00</updated><title type='text'>will,i want an autographed copy of your book!  i a...</title><content type='html'>will,&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;i want an autographed copy of your book!  i asked first.  no ladies in line? :-)  cool.  i got first dibs. :-)</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/116413198123573982/comments/default/116413413695395078'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/116413198123573982/comments/default/116413413695395078'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/11/review-of-news-november-21.html?showComment=1164134100000#c116413413695395078' title=''/><author><name>rick</name><uri>http://www.